    {
      "type": "frame",
      "id": "rl7Oc",
      "x": 6980,
      "y": 0,
      "name": "Chats · chat page · notes",
      "theme": {
        "mode": "dark"
      },
      "width": 720,
      "fill": "$surface",
      "stroke": "$border",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "layout": "vertical",
      "gap": 16,
      "padding": 32,
      "children": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "z8diN",
          "name": "title",
          "fill": "$text-primary",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "Chats per project: the chat page",
          "lineHeight": 1.1,
          "fontFamily": "$font-display",
          "fontSize": 28,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "YxcGq",
          "name": "Parti pris",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "layout": "vertical",
          "gap": 6,
          "padding": [
            8,
            0,
            0,
            0
          ],
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "G8dYi",
              "name": "caption",
              "fill": "$text-secondary",
              "content": "PARTI PRIS",
              "lineHeight": 1.2,
              "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
              "fontSize": 10,
              "fontWeight": "normal",
              "letterSpacing": 0.8
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "zveRo",
              "name": "line",
              "fill": "$text-primary",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "A chat is one conversation with the orchestrator of a project, on one topic, and every chat of the project shares its team. The page: the conversation; its head with the title, the project and number, and the team; and on the right what this chat delegated, to which agent, its state and its result, as T3 Code's thread relationships panel.",
              "lineHeight": 1.5,
              "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
              "fontSize": 14,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "oDZIT",
          "name": "The room",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "layout": "vertical",
          "gap": 6,
          "padding": [
            8,
            0,
            0,
            0
          ],
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "qWozS",
              "name": "caption",
              "fill": "$text-secondary",
              "content": "THE ROOM",
              "lineHeight": 1.2,
              "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
              "fontSize": 10,
              "fontWeight": "normal",
              "letterSpacing": 0.8
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "o0xET",
              "name": "line",
              "fill": "$text-primary",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "The current Chat stays as it is: the super orchestrator's space, which sees everything in every project, messages each project's orchestrator and receives their messages. Nothing about it is retired; the topic chats are added beside it.",
              "lineHeight": 1.5,
              "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
              "fontSize": 14,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "lZlXY",
              "name": "line",
              "fill": "$text-primary",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "In the new shell it is the fixed first entry above the chat list, Tars, all projects, which opens the Chat page unchanged. A chat's Room button, and Open the room on a project's page, lead to that project's room in this page. Since v2.2 the room shows what crosses it, what Tars and the project say to each other; a chat's conversation and its workers' notes to it stay in the chat.",
              "lineHeight": 1.5,
              "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
              "fontSize": 14,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "yblvV",
          "name": "Numbers",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "layout": "vertical",
          "gap": 6,
          "padding": [
            8,
            0,
            0,
            0
          ],
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "YR6Nt",
              "name": "caption",
              "fill": "$text-secondary",
              "content": "NUMBERS",
              "lineHeight": 1.2,
              "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
              "fontSize": 10,
              "fontWeight": "normal",
              "letterSpacing": 0.8
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "xN2Z1",
              "name": "line",
              "fill": "$text-primary",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "Every chat has a number fixed in its project: #1 is Main, the persistent orchestrator's chat, where Telegram and Hermes write; then #2, #3 and on, never reused. The row in the list says tars #3 and the head carries the same chip. Telegram prefixes each message with [tars #3 Fix the scroll lock], and a reply goes back to the chat it answers.",
              "lineHeight": 1.5,
              "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
              "fontSize": 14,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "Gm2b3",
          "name": "Chat · chats · orchestrator working",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "layout": "vertical",
          "gap": 6,
          "padding": [
            8,
            0,
            0,
            0
          ],
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "uPU1P",
              "name": "caption",
              "fill": "$text-secondary",
              "content": "CHAT · CHATS · ORCHESTRATOR WORKING",
              "lineHeight": 1.2,
              "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
              "fontSize": 10,
              "fontWeight": "normal",
              "letterSpacing": 0.8
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "RvbZi",
              "name": "line",
              "fill": "$text-primary",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "The orchestrator gave the fix to Frontend Engineer, with QA after it, and reads a file meanwhile: the line at the end of the thread says what it does and for how long. The panel shows both tasks; the chat reads working in the sidebar.",
              "lineHeight": 1.5,
              "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
              "fontSize": 14,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "KVBks",
          "name": "Chat · chats · a worker on another chat",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "layout": "vertical",
          "gap": 6,
          "padding": [
            8,
            0,
            0,
            0
          ],
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "gPcGq",
              "name": "caption",
              "fill": "$text-secondary",
              "content": "CHAT · CHATS · A WORKER ON ANOTHER CHAT",
              "lineHeight": 1.2,
              "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
              "fontSize": 10,
              "fontWeight": "normal",
              "letterSpacing": 0.8
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "RHy0y",
              "name": "line",
              "fill": "$text-primary",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "Backend Engineer is busy with another chat of the same project. The task this chat gave it waits in its queue, first in, first out: the line in the thread reads \"Backend Engineer is on 'Speed up the Usage scan' (since 10:31). Your request is 2nd in its queue.\", with a way to that chat, and the panel marks the task 2nd in queue.",
              "lineHeight": 1.5,
              "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
              "fontSize": 14,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "Dcli9",
          "name": "Chat · chats · a result back",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "layout": "vertical",
          "gap": 6,
          "padding": [
            8,
            0,
            0,
            0
          ],
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "bEskn",
              "name": "caption",
              "fill": "$text-secondary",
              "content": "CHAT · CHATS · A RESULT BACK",
              "lineHeight": 1.2,
              "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
              "fontSize": 10,
              "fontWeight": "normal",
              "letterSpacing": 0.8
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "KZyfb",
              "name": "line",
              "fill": "$text-primary",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "Frontend Engineer's result comes back into the thread as a card: what changed, how long it took, and the diff and its terminal one click away. The panel marks the task done with its result, and QA's task starts.",
              "lineHeight": 1.5,
              "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
              "fontSize": 14,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "L89HD3",
          "name": "Chat · chats · waiting on you",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "layout": "vertical",
          "gap": 6,
          "padding": [
            8,
            0,
            0,
            0
          ],
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "tvyHX",
              "name": "caption",
              "fill": "$text-secondary",
              "content": "CHAT · CHATS · WAITING ON YOU",
              "lineHeight": 1.2,
              "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
              "fontSize": 10,
              "fontWeight": "normal",
              "letterSpacing": 0.8
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "OhcBn",
              "name": "line",
              "fill": "$text-primary",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "The orchestrator asks a permission before it runs a command: the ask sits above the composer with the command, Deny and Allow. The chat moves to Active in the sidebar and reads waiting on you there.",
              "lineHeight": 1.5,
              "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
              "fontSize": 14,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "hEQ3W",
          "name": "Chat · chats · new chat",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "layout": "vertical",
          "gap": 6,
          "padding": [
            8,
            0,
            0,
            0
          ],
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "r9jiJ",
              "name": "caption",
              "fill": "$text-secondary",
              "content": "CHAT · CHATS · NEW CHAT",
              "lineHeight": 1.2,
              "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
              "fontSize": 10,
              "fontWeight": "normal",
              "letterSpacing": 0.8
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "yEH8D",
              "name": "line",
              "fill": "$text-primary",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "Pick the project, the current one already chosen, and write. The chat takes the project's next number (#5 here), and its first message gives it its title.",
              "lineHeight": 1.5,
              "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
              "fontSize": 14,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "JXrz3",
          "name": "Chat · chats · every slot working",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "layout": "vertical",
          "gap": 6,
          "padding": [
            8,
            0,
            0,
            0
          ],
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "JQmNE",
              "name": "caption",
              "fill": "$text-secondary",
              "content": "CHAT · CHATS · EVERY SLOT WORKING",
              "lineHeight": 1.2,
              "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
              "fontSize": 10,
              "fontWeight": "normal",
              "letterSpacing": 0.8
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "rhZOB",
              "name": "line",
              "fill": "$text-primary",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "A send while every slot holds a working chat is refused, as an error the user sees: \"3 chats are already working, the most this Mac runs at once (16 GB of RAM, one chat per 5 GB). Wait for one to finish, or stop one:\" Each working chat is named, opens its chat, and has its Stop. The message stays in the composer. The list's header reads 3 of 3 working. An idle chat is put to sleep without a word to free a slot; this error comes only when none can be freed.",
              "lineHeight": 1.5,
              "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
              "fontSize": 14,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "dLE31",
