    {
      "type": "frame",
      "id": "o931Y4",
      "x": 6980,
      "y": 8000,
      "name": "Chats · chat page from the transcripts · notes",
      "theme": {
        "mode": "dark"
      },
      "width": 720,
      "fill": "$surface",
      "stroke": "$border",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "layout": "vertical",
      "gap": 16,
      "padding": 32,
      "children": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "HgZPS",
          "name": "title",
          "fill": "$text-primary",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "The chat page, from its transcripts",
          "lineHeight": 1.1,
          "fontFamily": "$font-display",
          "fontSize": 28,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "Bx2kj",
          "name": "Parti pris",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "layout": "vertical",
          "gap": 6,
          "padding": [
            8,
            0,
            0,
            0
          ],
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "E7O3W",
              "name": "caption",
              "fill": "$text-secondary",
              "content": "PARTI PRIS",
              "lineHeight": 1.2,
              "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
              "fontSize": 10,
              "fontWeight": "normal",
              "letterSpacing": 0.8
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "G4zn0a",
              "name": "line",
              "fill": "$text-primary",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "A chat's page reads its conversation from its runner's transcripts (chat:history, #371) and follows it live from the seq it was read at (chat:events). Each line is shown as what it is: your words, the orchestrator's, its tool calls folded to a line, an agent's or a channel's message, a note from Tars or Claude Code, a divider where the conversation was compacted or a new session began, and a line Tars cannot read, as one muted line. It opens on the last 200 lines; Show earlier, above the first, reads the 200 before, and says how many lines are left.",
              "lineHeight": 1.5,
              "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
              "fontSize": 14,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "bfn6q",
          "name": "Chat · chats · from its transcripts, working",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "layout": "vertical",
          "gap": 6,
          "padding": [
            8,
            0,
            0,
            0
          ],
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "jTRJA",
              "name": "caption",
              "fill": "$text-secondary",
              "content": "CHAT · CHATS · FROM ITS TRANSCRIPTS, WORKING",
              "lineHeight": 1.2,
              "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
              "fontSize": 10,
              "fontWeight": "normal",
              "letterSpacing": 0.8
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "rkV6Z",
              "name": "line",
              "fill": "$text-primary",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "The runner in a turn: the line at the end of the thread says so, with its last tool call. Lines that arrive while the page is open take their place in the thread; a gap in the seq reads the conversation again.",
              "lineHeight": 1.5,
              "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
              "fontSize": 14,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "k5yfc9",
          "name": "Chat · chats · from its transcripts, waiting on you",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "layout": "vertical",
          "gap": 6,
          "padding": [
            8,
            0,
            0,
            0
          ],
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "v9iNI",
              "name": "caption",
              "fill": "$text-secondary",
              "content": "CHAT · CHATS · FROM ITS TRANSCRIPTS, WAITING ON YOU",
              "lineHeight": 1.2,
              "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
              "fontSize": 10,
              "fontWeight": "normal",
              "letterSpacing": 0.8
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "WKTGU",
              "name": "line",
              "fill": "$text-primary",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "The runner asks a permission: the ask sits above the composer as an agent's window shows it, and allow, deny or ask in terminal answers it there.",
              "lineHeight": 1.5,
              "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
              "fontSize": 14,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "Ug37p",
          "name": "Waiting for PR D",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "layout": "vertical",
          "gap": 6,
          "padding": [
            8,
            0,
            0,
            0
          ],
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "kx3J8",
              "name": "caption",
              "fill": "$text-secondary",
              "content": "SENDING",
              "lineHeight": 1.2,
              "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
              "fontSize": 10,
              "fontWeight": "normal",
              "letterSpacing": 0.8
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "mNowE",
              "name": "line",
              "fill": "$text-primary",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "The field sends through chat:send. A chat whose orchestrator runs has the words typed into it, and while it works they go in when its turn ends; something typed in its terminal holds them until that field is clear. A chat whose orchestrator does not run starts it with them: Main resumes its conversation, a new chat starts its own, in a worktree of its own (Chat · chats · a new chat, its first message). A refusal is said in the page, never dropped: every slot working draws its own, with who works and a Stop for each (Chat · chats · every slot working); any other reads Not sent with the reason, the words kept (Chat · chats · the composer, sending). The sidebar reads N of M working from system:chatLimit: M the limit this Mac's memory sets, N the chats whose orchestrator holds a terminal, its square idle at 0. What a chat delegated shows on the right once a task names the chat it came from.",
              "lineHeight": 1.5,
              "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
              "fontSize": 14,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
